<!--
  A phone with a pulse across it. Chosen by the product owner from four candidates rendered at the
  sizes an icon is actually met at, replacing a 3x3 grid whose dead centre cell was invisible at 24dp.

  ## Geometry, and the mistake that shaped the first attempt

  Body: 42 x 64 at x 33..75, y 22..86, corner 9.

  A launcher may mask an adaptive icon to a CIRCLE of diameter 72, so anything more than 36 from the
  centre can be cropped. The first version of this file used a 32 x 60 body because the corner was
  measured as hypot(w/2, h/2) - the SHARP corner. That is the wrong measurement for a rounded
  rectangle: the farthest point sits on the corner arc, at hypot(w/2-r, h/2-r) + r. For 42 x 64 with a
  9 radius that is 34.9, comfortably safe, where the sharp-corner estimate said 38.3 and rejected it.

  The cost of that error was visible rather than theoretical: the mark sat small in a sea of
  background and read as a battery or a domino rather than a phone. It is a third wider now.

  Pulse: stroke 8, inset 6 from each side, spanning x 39..69 about the centre line.

  Inset so the line has room rather than running edge to edge, which read as cramped. Stroke 8 because
  8/108 is about 1.8px at 24dp, and the pulse is the only part carrying meaning - if it disappears,
  the icon is a white slab.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#FAFAFA"
        android:pathData="M42,22h24a9,9 0 0,1 9,9v46a9,9 0 0,1 -9,9h-24a9,9 0 0,1 -9,-9V31a9,9 0 0,1 9,-9z" />

    <path
        android:strokeColor="#22C55E"
        android:strokeWidth="8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M39,54h4l4,-10l6,20l5,-10h6" />
</vector>
